meta {
  name: requests
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/requests
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.items: isArray
}

docs {
  One operation, two shapes, chosen by Accept — this request sends no
  Accept override, so it gets the JSON snapshot and completes immediately.
  `Accept: text/event-stream` on the same URL instead holds the connection
  open and streams one `data:` line per request recorded from that point;
  see requesttrackhttp's own handler tests for that path; a Bruno request
  cannot demonstrate it without hanging the collection for the length of
  the connection.

  items is never empty by the time this collection reaches this request —
  everything run so far (health, auth/login, users/create, ...) is itself
  in the buffer, this request included, once the *next* one runs.
}
